-- title:
--   Haar measure on the idele class group via a fundamental domain
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a number field, and equip the adele ring $\mathbb{A}_F$ of $F$ (relative to $\mathcal{O}_F$), its unit group $\mathbb{A}_F^\times$ and the relevant general linear groups with their Borel $\sigma$-algebras, the Borel structure being the one generated by the topology. Write $\Gamma = \mathrm{principalIdeles}$ for the subgroup of $\mathbb{A}_F^\times$ given by the image of $F^\times$ under the map of unit groups induced by $F \to \mathbb{A}_F$, and $C_F = \mathbb{A}_F^\times/\Gamma$ for the quotient group, carrying the quotient topology and, as explicitly bound in the statement, the Borel $\sigma$-algebra of that topology (not Mathlib's default quotient $\sigma$-algebra). Let $\mathrm{idelicHaar}$ denote the Haar measure `Measure.haar` on $\mathbb{A}_F^\times$. Given a set $D \subseteq \mathbb{A}_F^\times$ which is measurable and which is a fundamental domain for the action of $\Gamma$ with respect to $\mathrm{idelicHaar}$, the conclusion is fourfold: $C_F$ is Hausdorff, second countable and locally compact, and there exists a Haar measure $\nu$ on $C_F$ such that the pushforward of $\mathrm{idelicHaar}$ restricted to $D$ along the projection $\mathbb{A}_F^\times \to C_F$ equals $\nu$. No normalisation of $\nu$ is asserted.
--
--   This is the standard construction of Haar measure on the idele class group $C_F$ from Haar measure on $\mathbb{A}_F^\times$ together with a fundamental domain for the principal ideles, in the style of Weil and of Tate's thesis, packaged with the topological properties of $C_F$ needed to do measure theory on it. It is used in the analytic part of the development, in the approximation of $L^p$ functions on the idele classes by continuous ones.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_NumberField_Idele_t2Space_and_secondCountable_and_locallyCompact_and_exists_isHaarMeasure_map_mk_restrict_of_isFundamentalDomain.lean

